        "content": "<p>alexcrichton opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14773\">PR #14773</a> from <code>alexcrichton:oom-funcref-push</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This commit fixes an issue where when a new host function was inserted<br>\ninto the store if an OOM happened between two <code>push</code>-es on different<br>\nvectors it could leave the store in an inconsistent state with using the<br>\nwrong <code>VMFuncRef</code>. The fix here is to ensure that this is a bit more<br>\ntransactional where the entire function succeeds or fails rather than<br>\nonly partially succeeding.</p>\n</blockquote>",
